    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the road entrance to the access drive so responders can identify the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to define the turn-in point at night or in low visibility conditions.\n• Post a clearly visible property map or site diagram near the road entrance showing the location of the main residence and detached structure.\n• Keep the full length of the access drive clear of parked vehicles so responding units can reach the circular driveway without stopping.\n• Maintain the access drive width along its entire length to allow two emergency vehicles to pass or one large vehicle to navigate without leaving the roadway.\n• Trim any trees or shrubs along the access drive that hang low enough to obstruct a fire engine or ladder truck.\n• Keep the circular driveway clear of vehicles, equipment, and stored materials so arriving units can position without repositioning other apparatus.\n• Mark a designated turnaround or staging area on the property so responders arriving in large vehicles have a known exit path without backing a long distance.\n• Identify the detached structure with a clearly visible address or unit marker so responders can distinguish it from the main residence on arrival.\n• Keep a gate, if present at the single access point, unlocked or equipped with a knox box or standard emergency access lock."
  },
