    "recommendations": "• Trim shrubs that are growing directly next to the structure on all sides.\n• Thin scattered trees near the structure to increase open space between their canopies and the building.\n• Clear grass and low vegetation from the area immediately surrounding the structure.\n• Remove or cut back shrubs and tall grass growing along the edges of the driveway.\n• Trim tree branches that overhang or lean over the driveway to keep the full width and height clear for vehicle access.\n• Keep the driveway surface clear of fallen branches, leaves, and dry plant material that could block access.\n• Create a wider cleared area near the end of the driveway to allow emergency vehicles to turn around or reposition.\n• Cut grass in open areas close to the structure before it dries out seasonally.\n• Maintain separation between scattered shrub clusters and the structure by removing shrubs that have grown into the clear zone around the building."
